From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt DeVillier <matt.devillier@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:07:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg/PlatformGopPolicy: Load GOP driver and VBT
 from CBFS

[ouroBIOS: commit 1f9ab463057c of MrChromebox's edk2, without the files
that TianoCore's tree does not have (tools/edk2-import.py): 6 in
edk2/OuroBiosPkg]

With USE_PLATFORM_GOP, load IntelGopDriver.efi and vbt.bin from
coreboot's CBFS at runtime instead of embedding them in the payload,
so the payload no longer depends on the board's GOP driver or VBT.

After installing the GOP policy protocol, wrap the GOP driver in an
in-memory firmware volume and hand it to the DXE dispatcher with
ProcessFirmwareVolume(). The driver is then dispatched once its depex
is met, and the image security policy treats it as coming from a
firmware volume, like any other driver in the payload. GetVbtData()
returns the VBT loaded from CBFS directly, and the now unused
gBmpImageGuid is removed. A VBT without a $VBT signature is rejected.

GraphicsOutputDxe is now always included. It only binds when coreboot
provides a framebuffer, so it covers boards where coreboot initializes
graphics and does not add a GOP driver to CBFS.

Signed-off-by: Matt DeVillier <matt.devillier@gmail.com>
---
